s, such as ophthalmology applications. The Medical Solutions segment provides a range of medical grade technologies, including medical insufflators, pumps, and related disposables; imaging, identification and RFID solutions; advanced motion control solutions; and light engines, and integrated operating room technologies. The company was formerly known as GSI Group, Inc. and changed its name to Novanta Inc. in May 2016. Novanta Inc. was incorporated in 1968 and is based in Bedford, Massachusetts.","desc_src":"Yahoo Finance profile via yfinance (third-party)","sic":"3690","sic_desc":"Miscellaneous Electrical Machinery, Equipment & Supplies","sector":"Technology","industry":"Scientific & Technical Instruments","mcap":5373148672,"mcap_src":"Yahoo Finance profile (third-party, cached)","hq":"BEDFORD, MA","exchange":"XNAS","fy_end":"1231","cik":1076930,"state_inc":"A3","massive_note":"Massive ticker details not fetched yet (5 calls/min limit; filled in on a nightly run)","sec_asof":"2026-10-03"},"fin":{"available":true,"src":"SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts","asof":"2026-09-29","q":[{"end":"2023-09-29","rev":221503000.0,"rev_yoy":-0.7,"eps":0.59,"eps_yoy":-6.3,"ni":21223000.0,"ni_yoy":-5.6,"nm":9.6,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2023-12-31","rev":211569000.0,"rev_yoy":-3.1,"eps":0.34,"eps_yoy":-19.0,"ni":12511000.0,"ni_yoy":-18.0,"nm":5.9,"derived":["eps","rev","ni"],"fp":null},{"end":"2024-03-29","rev":230916000.0,"rev_yoy":5.4,"eps":0.41,"eps_yoy":-19.6,"ni":14676000.0,"ni_yoy":-19.6,"nm":6.4,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2024-06-28","rev":235864000.0,"rev_yoy":2.8,"eps":0.38,"eps_yoy":-34.5,"ni":13755000.0,"ni_yoy":-34.1,"nm":5.8,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2024-09-27","rev":244405000.0,"rev_yoy":10.3,"eps":0.53,"eps_yoy":-10.2,"ni":19192000.0,"ni_yoy":-9.6,"nm":7.9,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2024-12-31","rev":238060000.0,"rev_yoy":12.5,"eps":0.45,"eps_yoy":32.4,"ni":16464000.0,"ni_yoy":31.6,"nm":6.9,"derived":["eps","rev","ni"],"fp":null},{"end":"2025-